Mina (Docs): Heads up — PR #452 for function/tool calling docs has a couple of ambiguous examples around optional tool outputs and schema fallbacks. Need quick eyes before merge. TL;DR: add an explicit `null`-tolerant example and an SDK snippet showing .parseFallback(...) or .orElse(...).
Sam (SDK): Can you paste the example you're worried about?
Mina (Docs): Here — current docs show required `result: { items: string[] }` only. We should show two variants: (1) canonical successful tool response, (2) tool returns `{ result: null }` or omits field. Proposed short example:
```json
{
  "tool_call": {
    "name": "price_lookup",
    "output": {
      "prices": ["9.99","19.99"]
    }
  }
}
```
and fallback:
```json
{
  "tool_call": {
    "name": "price_lookup",
    "output": null
  }
}
```
Sam (SDK): For SDK snippet, propose:
```js
const res = await client.callTool("price_lookup", prompt);
// prefer parse but allow null
const parsed = sdk.parse(res, schema).orElse(() => ({ prices: [] }));
```
or with explicit fallback parser:
```js
const parsed = sdk.parse(res, schema).orIfNull(() => ({ prices: [] }));
```
Oleg (ML-engineer): +1 on showing parse fallback. Also add note about preserving provenance: if output null, return cached KV or call secondary model. Don't make it prescriptive, just show options.
Jess (PM): We should also add a small migration note: "old callers that expected always-present arrays should handle empty arrays and update evaluators". Also add a link to evaluators guidance (placeholder): https://redwood.dev/evals/fallbacks — we'll swap to canonical link before merge.
Mina (Docs): I'll add both examples and the SDK snippet. Also need a tiny test in docs CI to ensure codeblocks compile-ish. @CI Bot can you run `docs/snippets/validate_tool_snippets.sh`?
CI Bot: Running snippet linter... failed: 1 snippet with `orIfNull` not found in current SDK; suggest using `.orElse` variant. See logs: https://ci.redwood.dev/logs/1234
Sam (SDK): I'll add alias `orIfNull` in next patch or update snippet to `.orElse(() => ...)`. Prefer updating snippet to avoid CI flake.
Mina (Docs): OK I'll replace `orIfNull` with `.orElse(...)`, add migration blurb, and ping SDK for final quick review. Reviewers: @Sam (SDK) @Oleg (ML-engineer) @Jess (PM). ETA EOD.
Sam (SDK): :eyes: will review in ~2h.
Oleg (ML-engineer): :+1:
Jess (PM): Thanks — tiny docs change, big UX win.
